<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "Create New Field (by name)" dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Field/FormFieldDir`
    (FormFieldDir.cs + FormFieldDir.Designer.cs). The operator types a new field name
    (sanitised live against glm.fileRegex), optionally appends the current date and/or time,
    then saves — which creates the field directory and writes its initial files. Per AAP §0.3.3
    this is a faithful parity reimplementation of the current Windows Forms look, never a redesign:
    no new colours, no relayout, no UX changes.

    Window shell — mirrors FormFieldDir.Designer.cs:
      ClientSize 676 x 260       -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window).
      FormBorderStyle.None        -> SystemDecorations="None".
      ControlBox = false          -> covered by the borderless (SystemDecorations="None") shell.
      ShowInTaskbar = false       -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      (Fixed, not resizable)      -> CanResize="False".
      StartPosition CenterParent  -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner" (shown modally over FormGPS;
                                     this replaces the WinForms ScreenHelper reposition, which per the
                                     file spec is intentionally NOT ported).
      Font Tahoma 14.25pt         -> FontFamily="Tahoma" + FontSize="19". WinForms points are converted
                                     to Avalonia device-independent pixels (pt x 96/72): 14.25 -> 19,
                                     18 -> 24. Because the window is sized 676 x 260 in DIP (1:1 with the
                                     WinForms client px), converting the fonts keeps the original physical
                                     proportions (same convention as the sibling FormYesView).
      BackColor Gainsboro         -> Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}". Per this file's spec the
                                     neutral chrome is themed to the App.axaml day/night palette rather
                                     than hard-coding a WinForms colour.
      Text "Create New Field "    -> Title (design-time; the code-behind assigns gStr.gsCreateNewField).

    Wiring contract — the partner code-behind (FormFieldDirView.axaml.cs) owns ALL behaviour:
      * Code-behind dialog: NO DataContext, NO x:DataType, NO MVVM bindings — exactly like the sibling
        FormYesView / FormInputDialogView. Controls are addressed imperatively by their x:Name.
      * Button Click handlers are declared here (OnAddDateClick / OnAddTimeClick / OnCancelClick /
        OnSaveClick) following the established OnXxxClick convention (e.g. FormYesView.axaml.cs:
        `private void OnOkClick(object sender, RoutedEventArgs e)`). The code-behind implements them,
        reproducing btnAddDate_Click (append " yyyy-MM-dd"), btnAddTime_Click (append " HH-mm"),
        btnSerialCancel_Click (Close) and btnSave_Click (create the field directory + files).
      * tboxFieldName declares NO events here: its TextChanged (glm.fileRegex sanitisation, then enable/
        disable btnSave on a non-empty trimmed name) and its tap -> on-screen keyboard
        (FormGPS.isKeyboardOn) flow are attached in the code-behind by name, mirroring FormFieldDir.cs.
      * btnSave starts IsEnabled="False" (WinForms FormFieldDir_Load: btnSave.Enabled = false); the
        code-behind enables it once the trimmed name is non-empty.
      * The "Enter Field Name" and "+" texts below are design-time placeholders; at runtime the
        code-behind assigns labelEnterFieldName.Text = gStr.gsEnterFieldName.

    Colours come from App.axaml's day/night ThemeDictionaries via {DynamicResource ...} (so the live
    Light<->Dark switch is observed) — no WinForms colours, no GDI namespaces. Button glyphs are served
    from the GPS assembly (assembly name "AgOpenGPS") via avares:// URIs (OK64 / Cancel64 /
    JobNameCalendar / JobNameTime, each a native 64 x 64 PNG) — the convention used by every sibling
    GPS view.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.FormFieldDirView"
        Title="Create New Field"
        Width="676"
        Height="260"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        FontSize="19"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}">

    <!--
        Flat, borderless, transparent image buttons — the cross-platform equivalent of the WinForms
        FlatStyle.Flat + FlatAppearance.BorderSize = 0 + BackColor = Transparent carried by every button
        in FormFieldDir.Designer.cs. The Fluent Button template otherwise paints a hover / pressed /
        disabled fill; these setters keep the face transparent in all interaction states so only the
        64 x 64 glyph shows (the same technique used by the sibling FormYesView and Keypad/NumKeypad).
        The :disabled face stays transparent too; the Fluent template still dims the glyph, reproducing
        the greyed look of the WinForms disabled btnSave.
    -->
    <Window.Styles>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <!-- Disabled image buttons render their glyph dimmed, reproducing the greyed look WinForms
             applies to a disabled Button.Image (e.g. the initially-disabled btnSave). An Avalonia
             <Image> is unaffected by the Fluent theme's disabled foreground, so the dim is applied
             explicitly here via Opacity; it reverts to full opacity the moment the code-behind sets
             btnSave.IsEnabled = true on a non-empty trimmed name. -->
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:disabled">
            <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.5" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.flatImage:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Three logical bands (mirrors the designer): the name label + textbox across the top, then a
        single action band that — exactly like the WinForms layout — places the two "+ date / + time"
        append controls on the LEFT and the Cancel / Save buttons on the RIGHT. The designer overlaps
        these two groups vertically inside the 260px height (add buttons y116-195, Cancel/Save y161-240),
        so they share one band rather than stacking; the left group is vertically centred and the right
        group bottom-aligned to reproduce that staggered arrangement.
    -->
    <Grid Margin="24,18,18,14">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />   <!-- labelEnterFieldName : designer (34,25)        -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />   <!-- tboxFieldName       : designer (27,51) 634x36  -->
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />      <!-- action band         : add (left) + Save/Cancel (right) -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- labelEnterFieldName: Tahoma 14.25pt Bold (-> 19 DIP). Runtime text = gStr.gsEnterFieldName. -->
        <TextBlock x:Name="labelEnterFieldName"
                   Grid.Row="0"
                   Text="Enter Field Name"
                   FontSize="19"
                   FontWeight="Bold"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                   HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                   Margin="0,0,0,8" />

        <!-- tboxFieldName: Tahoma 18pt Bold (-> 24 DIP), single line, stretched across the dialog
             (designer 634 wide). This is the focal control. Its TextChanged (sanitisation + btnSave
             enable) and tap -> on-screen keyboard flow are wired in the code-behind, so no events are
             declared here. The WinForms BackColor (AliceBlue) is intentionally NOT hard-coded — the
             Fluent theme supplies the day/night-aware input background (no WinForms colours). -->
        <TextBox x:Name="tboxFieldName"
                 Grid.Row="1"
                 FontSize="24"
                 FontWeight="Bold"
                 MinHeight="44"
                 HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                 VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                 AutomationProperties.Name="Field name" />

        <!-- Action band: add controls (left) + Save/Cancel (right) share one row. -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="2">

            <!--
                LEFT: the two "append to name" controls, each a "+" label followed by its image button
                (designer: label2 + btnAddDate, label3 + btnAddTime). btnAddDate appends the date
                (yyyy-MM-dd) and btnAddTime appends the time (HH-mm) — handled in the code-behind.
            -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center"
                        Spacing="32">

                <!-- + date -->
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                            Spacing="4"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="label2"
                               Text="+"
                               FontSize="19"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    <Button x:Name="btnAddDate"
                            Classes="flatImage"
                            Width="83"
                            Height="79"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Add date"
                            Click="OnAddDateClick">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/JobNameCalendar.png"
                               Width="64"
                               Height="64"
                               Stretch="Uniform" />
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>

                <!-- + time -->
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                            Spacing="4"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="label3"
                               Text="+"
                               FontSize="19"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    <Button x:Name="btnAddTime"
                            Classes="flatImage"
                            Width="83"
                            Height="79"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Add time"
                            Click="OnAddTimeClick">
                        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/JobNameTime.png"
                               Width="64"
                               Height="64"
                               Stretch="Uniform" />
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>

            </StackPanel>

            <!--
                RIGHT: Cancel then Save (designer order: btnSerialCancel @ x=457, btnSave @ x=573),
                bottom-aligned. btnSave starts disabled (WinForms FormFieldDir_Load) and is enabled by
                the code-behind once a non-empty trimmed name is present.
            -->
            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal"
                        HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                        VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                        Spacing="12">
                <Button x:Name="btnSerialCancel"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Width="77"
                        Height="79"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel"
                        Click="OnCancelClick">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png"
                           Width="64"
                           Height="64"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>
                <Button x:Name="btnSave"
                        Classes="flatImage"
                        Width="83"
                        Height="79"
                        IsEnabled="False"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Save"
                        Click="OnSaveClick">
                    <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                           Width="64"
                           Height="64"
                           Stretch="Uniform" />
                </Button>
            </StackPanel>

        </Grid>
    </Grid>
</Window>
